eproduce the bug organically and had to add special testing logic to SQLite that deliberately triggers the circumstances of the the bug in order to verify that the issue has been fixed.replyAriarule 9 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Odd not to highlight the sentence where they answer the obvious question \"Why Tailscale in particular?\":> They also explained why we were more likely to hit the bug than other SQLite users: we take manual control of the checkpointing process, and we checkpoint very aggressively. Even a bug triggered by a rare condition was bound to hit us eventually.replynoncoml 9 minutes ago | prev [–] How come mythos didn’t find this?reply Guidelines | FAQ | Lists | API | Security | Legal | Apply to YC | Contact Search:\n=== END PAGE TEXT ===\n\nGoal: Visit Hacker News and:\n1. Identify the top story on the front page (the first article in the list)\n2. Drill into its comments thread\n3. Record the story title (key=story_title) and story URL (key=story_url) in working memory\n4. Record your summary of the top 3 comments as key=top_comments (one paragraph, 2-3 sentences)\n5. Call terminate(finalAnswer=...) with a one-paragraph summary including the story title and a synthesis of what commenters are saying",
